# Kit, without any claim (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Claims in someone else's kit"): people react to what
# you wear. Your own colours suit you; theirs on a stranger get a question, never an accusation.
# There's no disguise with the Haven (its mark is the bear on its doors, not on its people).
# Greet lines are conditional (the talk screen shows only a line that says something).

conv named.bastion.kit_own
for named:bastion
when kit:own
greet
voice bastion
daily

node start
  say? kit:own :: Kit suits you. Mind the collar. The sergeant notices collars, and the sergeant notices who's in Bastion green at {here} that wasn't on this morning's roster.

conv named.bastion.kit_theirs
for named:bastion
when kit:in_kit & !passing
greet
voice bastion
daily

node start
  say? kit:in_kit :: Where did you get that jacket? Don't answer. If you answer I have to write it down, and if I write it down somebody has to come out and ask you properly.

conv named.redhand.kit_own
for named:redhand
when kit:own
greet
voice redhand
daily

node start
  say? kit:own :: Wearing the red. Good. Now everyone on the road knows who to blame, and who to pay. Mostly who to pay. Blame's free, and we don't do free.

conv named.redhand.kit_theirs
for named:redhand
when kit:in_kit & !passing
greet
voice redhand
daily

node start
  say? kit:in_kit :: Nice armband. Whose was it before? Doesn't matter. Everything out here was somebody's before. The book usually says whose, and what they paid for it.

conv named.halcyon.kit_theirs
for named:halcyon
when kit:in_kit & !passing
greet
voice halcyon
daily

node start
  say? kit:in_kit :: That coat has someone's initials in the collar and a notebook number on the cuff. Neither of them is yours. I am noting it, for the record. Everything here goes in a record.
